le/lo with numbers work like fractions.

1 / 3 dogs (one of three dogs) = pa lo ci gerku ku
? / 3 dogs (some number out of three dogs) = lo ci gerku ku
1 / ? dogs (one of some number of dogs) = pa lo gerku ku

As far as numbering is concerned, you can use KOhA referents, you can say 
{le pluta xi pa}, which is adding a subscript 1, or you can just say {le 
pamoi pluta}, "the first path". Those are your options AFAIK. Why do you not 
want to use {moi}?

